Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.75,0:00:09.24,Main,Mio,0,0,0,,I had never even dreamed \Nof the sight I saw that day.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.38,0:00:13.37,Main,Mio,0,0,0,,Even now, after so, so long,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.17,0:00:16.95,Main,Mio,0,0,0,,my memory of it hasn't faded in the slightest.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.01,0:00:20.98,Main,Mio,0,0,0,,But how I've longed to see him,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.49,0:00:25.47,Main,Mio,0,0,0,,even if it were only in a dream...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.03,0:00:29.50,Main,Mio,0,0,0,,I miss him.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.90,0:00:31.37,Main,Mio,0,0,0,,I want to see him one more time...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.14,0:00:45.35,Main,CloneA,0,0,0,,Am I...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.35,0:00:46.66,Main,CloneB,0,0,0,,All right?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.21,0:00:48.46,Main,Kurumi,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.46,0:00:50.71,Main,Kurumi,0,0,0,,More importantly, is Ms. Murasame...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.13,0:00:53.53,Main,Kurumi,0,0,0,,No, is Phantom nearby?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.15,0:00:56.59,Main,CloneC,0,0,0,,She's nowhere in the vicinity.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.59,0:00:59.21,Main,CloneA,0,0,0,,It would seem she's disappeared.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.80,0:01:02.19,Main,Kurumi,0,0,0,,That was too easy.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.19,0:01:05.93,Main,Kurumi,0,0,0,,Though a Spirit that's divided its power\Ntoo greatly wouldn't amount to much more.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.46,0:01:14.21,Main,Kurumi,0,0,0,,However, defeating Phantom doesn't \Nmean I've achieved my goal.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.88,0:01:18.09,Main,CloneB,0,0,0,,Yes, yes. Of course not.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.09,0:01:22.96,Main,CloneC,0,0,0,,Our goal isn't the present fragmented fool.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.96,0:01:26.56,Main,CloneC,0,0,0,,It's the monster of the past\Nat its full power.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.98,0:01:33.44,Main,CloneA,0,0,0,,Still, why would Phantom divide \Nher power to create more Spirits?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.10,0:01:37.97,Main,CloneA,0,0,0,,She must have known that would \Ninevitably spell her own decline.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.82,0:01:44.40,Main,Kotori,0,0,0,,So you're saying Kurumi \Nhas saved you over 204 times?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.40,0:01:45.20,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.66,0:01:47.28,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,Every time I got killed,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.28,0:01:51.09,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,she rewound time and stopped DEM's attack.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.46,0:01:55.02,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,Kurumi's goal is to go back in time \Nand defeat the Spirit of Origin
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.02,0:01:57.85,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,in order to save her best friend.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.63,0:02:03.72,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,She also means to prevent all tragedy \Ncaused by Spirits before it ever happens.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.27,0:02:07.51,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,And she needs my Spirit power to do that.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.73,0:02:13.63,Main,Tohka,0,0,0,,I can't believe that's what was \Ngoing on with Kurumi...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.63,0:02:15.99,Main,Yoshino,0,0,0,,I'm surprised.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.33,0:02:19.05,Main,Miku,0,0,0,,So even the Sephirah within each of us
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.05,0:02:24.45,Main,Miku,0,0,0,,were refined at the cost of \Ncountless human lives...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.45,0:02:27.42,Main,Miku,0,0,0,,I have mixed feelings about that.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.96,0:02:31.50,Main,Kotori,0,0,0,,Whatever Kurumi's reasons may be,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.50,0:02:34.35,Main,Kotori,0,0,0,,we can't afford to hand over\N Shido's Spirit power.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.35,0:02:35.96,Main,Kotori,0,0,0,,That comes above all else.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.96,0:02:37.12,Main,Kotori,0,0,0,,For one thing,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.12,0:02:41.45,Main,Kotori,0,0,0,,we don't have any guarantee that Kurumi \Ncan even defeat this Spirit of Origin.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.45,0:02:44.85,Main,Mana,0,0,0,,Her story's also hard for me to believe.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.14,0:02:49.91,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,That's right. You've fought Kurumi \Nplenty of times already.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.91,0:02:50.37,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,But—
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.37,0:02:51.35,Main,Mana,0,0,0,,Even so!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.35,0:02:56.68,Main,Mana,0,0,0,,If you ask me if it's {\i1}more{\i0} likely\N that you're lying to me, big brother,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.68,0:02:59.49,Main,Mana,0,0,0,,then I'm forced to believe you two \Nby a narrow margin.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.82,0:03:01.90,Main,Natsumi,0,0,0,,This is getting complicated.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.90,0:03:04.99,Main,Natsumi,0,0,0,,Though I understand what you're getting at.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.30,0:03:07.12,Main,Mana,0,0,0,,More importantly, big brother,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.12,0:03:10.16,Main,Mana,0,0,0,,there's one other thing \NI'm very concerned about.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.16,0:03:11.00,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,Hmm?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.00,0:03:15.50,Main,Mana,0,0,0,,This Mio Takamiya woman \Nthat came up in your story.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.94,0:03:19.26,Main,Mana,0,0,0,,I find it hard to believe \Nshe's unrelated to you and me.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.26,0:03:21.39,Main,Mana,0,0,0,,If her last name really is Takamiya,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.39,0:03:25.62,Main,Mana,0,0,0,,then there's a chance she's family.\N A blood relative.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.09,0:03:27.89,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,I was curious about that too.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.60,0:03:31.40,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,Who is this Mio Takamiya?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.40,0:03:34.15,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,And what is she creating Spirits for?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.58,0:03:37.40,Main,Kotori,0,0,0,,She gave Kurumi her Sephirah \Nand made her a Spirit.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.01,0:03:41.90,Main,Kotori,0,0,0,,Sounds like the Phantom \Nthat appeared before us.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.32,0:03:43.94,Main,Kaguya,0,0,0,,Mio Takamiya...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.94,0:03:45.15,Main,Kaguya,0,0,0,,Phantom...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.15,0:03:48.09,Main,Kaguya,0,0,0,,And the Spirit of Origin \Nthat Kurumi mentioned...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.68,0:03:49.71,Main,Yuzuru,0,0,0,,Question.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.71,0:03:54.00,Main,Yuzuru,0,0,0,,What is the relationship between all three?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.63,0:03:58.33,Main,Nia,0,0,0,,If only we could use my Raziel...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.33,0:04:01.04,Main,Nia,0,0,0,,Then we'd have our answer in an instant.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.04,0:04:04.30,Main,Mukuro,0,0,0,,Indeed, it's a peculiar story, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.64,0:04:07.64,Main,Mukuro,0,0,0,,If you're so curious,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.64,0:04:10.93,Main,Mukuro,0,0,0,,all you have to do is \Nremember your past, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.29,0:04:13.56,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,If only I could.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.38,0:04:17.72,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,But both Mana and I have lost \Nour memories.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.18,0:04:23.06,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,We don't even know a single \Nthing about why we lost them.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.06,0:04:25.70,Main,Mukuro,0,0,0,,You told me that before.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.11,0:04:29.33,Main,Mukuro,0,0,0,,That's why I'm saying \Nyou should try remembering.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.74,0:04:32.71,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,You think I can?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.71,0:04:35.68,Main,Mukuro,0,0,0,,My Michael is an absolute key.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.68,0:04:37.71,Main,Mukuro,0,0,0,,There's nothing it can't open.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.71,0:04:42.46,Main,Mukuro,0,0,0,,Not even the door to your sealed memories.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.46,0:04:45.63,Main,Natsumi,0,0,0,,Hold on!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.63,0:04:47.72,Main,Natsumi,0,0,0,,Is it safe to do something like that?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.72,0:04:50.72,Main,Miku,0,0,0,,I don't know what happened in the past,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.00,0:04:52.89,Main,Miku,0,0,0,,but it won't harm Darling
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.89,0:04:55.71,Main,Miku,0,0,0,,the moment he remembers, will it?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.13,0:04:57.13,Main,Mana,0,0,0,,Big brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.67,0:04:58.90,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,I'll be all right.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.90,0:05:00.11,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,Don't worry.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.81,0:05:03.11,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,This isn't just about\Nour connection to Mio Takamiya.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.54,0:05:06.11,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,I want to know what happened in our past
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.41,0:05:09.27,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,more than anyone else.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.09,0:05:12.35,Main,Kotori,0,0,0,,Shido...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.29,0:05:14.21,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,Michael!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.22,0:05:21.01,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,Okay, here I go.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.01,0:05:21.81,Main,Tohka,0,0,0,,Yeah!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.59,0:05:24.14,Main,Mukuro,0,0,0,,Don't worry.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.14,0:05:26.05,Main,Mukuro,0,0,0,,Believe in Michael.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.18,0:05:30.69,Main,Miku,0,0,0,,Such a long, hard object is going into Darling!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.69,0:05:33.14,Main,Kotori,0,0,0,,Miku, be quiet for a bit.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.69,0:05:33.87,Main - Top,Miku,0,0,0,,No! You can't! Don't!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.10,0:06:06.38,Main,Reine,0,0,0,,Oh, you've awakened, Shin.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.38,0:06:07.38,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,Wha?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.64,0:06:10.23,Main,Reine,0,0,0,,Hmm? Is something wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.01,0:06:14.02,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,Oh, no, it's nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.46,0:06:15.39,Main,Tohka,0,0,0,,Shido!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.21,0:06:17.55,Main,Tohka,0,0,0,,Are you okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.55,0:06:18.59,Main,Kotori,0,0,0,,Shido!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.59,0:06:21.11,Main,Yoshino,0,0,0,,Please take it easy.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.11,0:06:23.17,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,What's this now?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.17,0:06:24.36,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,What's going on?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.67,0:06:26.57,Main,Kaguya,0,0,0,,What do you mean, "What's going on"?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.57,0:06:29.38,Main,Kaguya,0,0,0,,You suddenly collapsed and gave us a fright!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.38,0:06:30.49,Main,Yuzuru,0,0,0,,Agreed.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.49,0:06:32.96,Main,Yuzuru,0,0,0,,After inserting Michael into your head,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.96,0:06:34.94,Main,Yuzuru,0,0,0,,you passed out.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.94,0:06:35.66,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.11,0:06:39.50,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,I see. Sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.50,0:06:41.23,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,Guess I worried you all.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.23,0:06:43.54,Main,Kotori,0,0,0,,No, what matters is you woke up.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.87,0:06:45.40,Main,Origami,0,0,0,,I knew my kiss would work.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.81,0:06:47.31,Main,Origami,0,0,0,,It woke Sleeping Beauty.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.31,0:06:47.86,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.55,0:06:50.91,Main,Kotori,0,0,0,,What nonsense are you spouting now?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.91,0:06:52.95,Main,Kotori,0,0,0,,Don't listen to her, Shido.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.95,0:06:54.53,Main,Origami,0,0,0,,Wait a minute now.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.53,0:06:57.81,Main,Origami,0,0,0,,There are numerous particles\N floating in this space,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.09,0:07:03.09,Main,Origami,0,0,0,,so you can't say for certain that ones \Nfrom my breath didn't reach Shido's.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.44,0:07:07.79,Main,Origami,0,0,0,,So I see no problem with regarding\N this as an indirect kiss.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.79,0:07:09.84,Main,Miku,0,0,0,,Hold it right there, Professor!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.84,0:07:14.70,Main,Miku,0,0,0,,That would mean that me and everyone \Nin this same room have been...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.07,0:07:18.04,Main,Origami,0,0,0,,Deeply entwined in a deep kiss.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.04,0:07:20.72,Main,Miku,0,0,0,,I can't believe such genius lies here!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.72,0:07:23.67,Main,Miku,0,0,0,,What has the scientific world \Nbeen doing this whole time?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.67,0:07:27.16,Main,Tohka,0,0,0,,Hold on. I'm not following now.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.16,0:07:29.37,Main,Tohka,0,0,0,,Just how are we all entwined?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.37,0:07:31.81,Main,Miku,0,0,0,,I'll explain it in practice later!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.81,0:07:34.30,Main,Miku,0,0,0,,While Natsumi joins us for a three-way!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.69,0:07:37.47,Main - Top,Natsumi,0,0,0,,Could you not rope me into this too?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.02,0:07:37.47,Main,Mukuro,0,0,0,,I'm sorry, Master.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.47,0:07:40.95,Main,Mukuro,0,0,0,,This was all because \NI suggested using Michael.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.95,0:07:44.29,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,Oh, no. Nothing's actually wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.29,0:07:46.19,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,See? I'm just fine!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.13,0:07:48.69,Main,Mukuro,0,0,0,,Master...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.69,0:07:50.41,Main,Mana,0,0,0,,So, big brother,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.41,0:07:52.03,Main,Mana,0,0,0,,what happened?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.03,0:07:54.27,Main,Mana,0,0,0,,Did you remember anything?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.27,0:07:55.49,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,Well, I...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.38,0:07:59.45,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,Huh? That's odd.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.78,0:08:02.53,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,I'm certain I saw something.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.02,0:08:05.85,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,Yet I can't remember anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.82,0:08:11.29,Main,Reine,0,0,0,,There's no need to hurry, Shin.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.02,0:08:14.55,Main,Reine,0,0,0,,You can just think of another way.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.39,0:08:16.86,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,Reine...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.86,0:08:20.77,Main,Mana,0,0,0,,Then could you try it on me too, big brother?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.77,0:08:21.71,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.71,0:08:26.27,Main,Mana,0,0,0,,It might not have worked for you, \Nbut I might be able to remember something.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.27,0:08:29.26,Main,Mana,0,0,0,,Whether it's about Mio Takamiya
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.26,0:08:32.01,Main,Mana,0,0,0,,or whatever happened to us in the past.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.01,0:08:32.85,Main,Kotori,0,0,0,,Yeah, yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.85,0:08:34.86,Main,Kotori,0,0,0,,We'll try that later, okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.86,0:08:37.87,Main,Kotori,0,0,0,,Right now, let's wait \Nfor Shido to recover first.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.87,0:08:38.85,Main,Mana,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.85,0:08:40.53,Main,Mana,0,0,0,,What's the big idea?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.58,0:08:44.01,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,She's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.01,0:08:45.16,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,I'm sorry, Mana.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.16,0:08:46.92,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,Can we try it another time?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.46,0:08:48.37,Main,Mana,0,0,0,,Hmm?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.58,0:08:54.07,Main,Ellen,0,0,0,,Ike, you said you found something?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.55,0:08:57.25,Main,Westcott,0,0,0,,How has Nightmare, Kurumi Tokisaki,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.25,0:09:01.42,Main,Westcott,0,0,0,,been able to interfere \Nwith every one of our attacks?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.20,0:09:06.76,Main,Westcott,0,0,0,,She's been aware of our plans in advance.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.16,0:09:10.59,Main,Westcott,0,0,0,,To be precise,\Nshe's actually experienced them,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.59,0:09:13.61,Main,Westcott,0,0,0,,then altered things each time
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.92,0:09:17.36,Main,Westcott,0,0,0,,to avoid Shido Itsuka's death.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.36,0:09:18.19,Main,Ellen,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.74,0:09:21.29,Main,Artemisia,0,0,0,,That would spell trouble.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.78,0:09:24.44,Main,Artemisia,0,0,0,,It means we'll always be a step behind.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.44,0:09:25.55,Main,Westcott,0,0,0,,Indeed.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.06,0:09:28.59,Main,Westcott,0,0,0,,Though we're not necessarily\Nat a disadvantage.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.50,0:09:32.53,Main,Westcott,0,0,0,,Any strategy we conduct several times,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.53,0:09:35.17,Main,Westcott,0,0,0,,Nightmare will have to face \Nseveral hundred times.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.51,0:09:39.73,Main,Westcott,0,0,0,,Repeating the same thing \Nover and over will exhaust her mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.73,0:09:45.64,Main,Westcott,0,0,0,,Even Nightmare can't have \Nendless stamina and willpower.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.10,0:09:50.31,Main,Ellen,0,0,0,,Are you suggesting we wait \Nuntil Nightmare gives up?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.01,0:09:53.40,Main,Westcott,0,0,0,,That's our most certain option.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.66,0:09:56.50,Main,Westcott,0,0,0,,However, there's still a chance
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.50,0:10:01.51,Main,Westcott,0,0,0,,Nightmare could come up with \Nsome solution we won't be able to think of.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.51,0:10:04.37,Main,Westcott,0,0,0,,So we should also do everything in our power
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.37,0:10:07.54,Main,Westcott,0,0,0,,to ensure she gives up as soon as possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.07,0:10:12.18,Main,NibeelcoleA,0,0,0,,Father, Father!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.18,0:10:13.38,Main,NibeelcoleA,0,0,0,,Look, look!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.38,0:10:14.92,Main,NibeelcoleB,0,0,0,,We caught this.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.34,0:10:16.68,Main,Both,0,0,0,,Nightmare!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.68,0:10:18.45,Main,Westcott,0,0,0,,Eavesdropping, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.45,0:10:20.44,Main,Westcott,0,0,0,,Well done, Nibeelcole.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.08,0:10:24.60,Main,NibeelcoleA,0,0,0,,But several people she was with got away.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.60,0:10:28.31,Main,NibeelcoleB,0,0,0,,They might have overheard your conversation.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.31,0:10:30.36,Main,Westcott,0,0,0,,What's wrong with that?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.36,0:10:34.53,Main,Westcott,0,0,0,,Let's have an all-out war with full knowledge\N of each other's capabilities.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.19,0:10:37.90,Main,Westcott,0,0,0,,There's still at least one of you left, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.40,0:10:40.82,Main,Westcott,0,0,0,,Tell your master for me...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.33,0:10:45.51,Main,Westcott,0,0,0,,I {\i1}will{\i0} kill Itsuka Shido.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.08,0:10:49.50,Main,Westcott,0,0,0,,No matter how many times you go back in time.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.50,0:10:52.25,Main,Westcott,0,0,0,,No matter how often you redo this world
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.76,0:10:56.20,Main,Westcott,0,0,0,,or how often you rewrite history.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.20,0:11:00.06,Main,Westcott,0,0,0,,I'll be so thorough that\Nthere's no overturning it.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.68,0:11:03.71,Main,Westcott,0,0,0,,Now, struggle all you like,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.93,0:11:07.32,Main,Westcott,0,0,0,,vilest Spirit.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.81,0:11:16.61,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,I was relieved Mana \Nbacked down for us yesterday.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.61,0:11:20.36,Main,Kotori,0,0,0,,She had her magic power\N enhanced by DEM, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.66,0:11:22.93,Main,Kotori,0,0,0,,If she'd recalled those memories too,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.93,0:11:25.21,Main,Kotori,0,0,0,,it would have been pretty damaging.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.21,0:11:28.37,Main,Kotori,0,0,0,,Even if we want intel on Mio Takamiya.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.73,0:11:30.86,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,Mio Takamiya, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.19,0:11:33.56,Main - Italics,Shido,0,0,0,,I wonder why...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.56,0:11:37.27,Main - Italics,Shido,0,0,0,,I feel sure I've known \Nthat name for a long time now.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.68,0:11:43.96,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,Kurumi!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.96,0:11:48.01,Main,PatchKurumi,0,0,0,,Good day, Shido, Kotori.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.30,0:11:50.05,Main,Kotori,0,0,0,,Good morning, Kurumi.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.05,0:11:53.05,Main,Kotori,0,0,0,,You're wearing an awfully \Nnice outfit today, aren't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.05,0:11:54.27,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,It's her clone.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.02,0:11:56.91,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,Thank you for last night.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.91,0:11:58.44,Main,PatchKurumi,0,0,0,,I should thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.44,0:12:02.43,Main,PatchKurumi,0,0,0,,But it's still too early for you\N to be thanking me.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.43,0:12:03.16,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.56,0:12:09.41,Main,PatchKurumi,0,0,0,,On February 20th, DEM Industries \Nwill use their full forces
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.82,0:12:12.13,Main,PatchKurumi,0,0,0,,to come kill you, Shido.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.73,0:12:17.17,Main,PatchKurumi,0,0,0,,I came here today to warn you of that.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.37,0:12:21.80,Main,Kotori,0,0,0,,So, what's your objective?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.18,0:12:24.41,Main,PatchKurumi,0,0,0,,To be honest,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.41,0:12:30.93,Main,PatchKurumi,0,0,0,,the main body of Kurumi Tokisaki doesn't \Nknow that I, her clone, am here right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.50,0:12:37.27,Main,PatchKurumi,0,0,0,,The real me intends to handle \Nthis matter all on our own.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.70,0:12:40.82,Main,PatchKurumi,0,0,0,,She plans to repeat time as often as it takes
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.82,0:12:44.41,Main,PatchKurumi,0,0,0,,to seize a future in which Shido survives.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.07,0:12:49.67,Main,PatchKurumi,0,0,0,,However, our enemy is aware of her resolve.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.67,0:12:52.01,Main,PatchKurumi,0,0,0,,That's why they're using their full forces.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.01,0:12:54.08,Main,PatchKurumi,0,0,0,,DEM's operation
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.08,0:12:59.69,Main,PatchKurumi,0,0,0,,is also an attempt to break my spirit \Nas I pass through time.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.81,0:13:06.47,Main,Kotori,0,0,0,,So the real reason you're here is \Nto encourage Shido to evacuate?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.47,0:13:09.97,Main,PatchKurumi,0,0,0,,That alone is not the entirety of the truth.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.97,0:13:10.72,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.40,0:13:14.69,Main,PatchKurumi,0,0,0,,It would be a waste for Shido \Nto remain in the dark
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.69,0:13:20.69,Main,PatchKurumi,0,0,0,,when I'm working so hard \Nto protect him, wouldn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.39,0:13:23.61,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,I get it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.70,0:13:28.45,Main,PatchKurumi,0,0,0,,Now, if you'll excuse me.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.45,0:13:32.08,Main,PatchKurumi,0,0,0,,Please do survive this, Shido.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.38,0:13:33.07,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,Kurumi!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.77,0:13:36.08,Main,PatchKurumi,0,0,0,,Yes, what is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.36,0:13:39.58,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,If it's possible, tell Kurumi:
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.02,0:13:43.83,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,"Thank you. I'm still alive because of you.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.37,0:13:47.47,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,But I won't be the one \Nin need of saving forever.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.79,0:13:51.93,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,Once we've taken care of DEM, \NI'll come to seal your Spirit power—"
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.83,0:13:54.06,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,No, that's not right.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.30,0:13:59.18,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,"This time, I'll be the one to steal a kiss.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.90,0:14:02.50,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,So prepare yourself, my honey."
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.11,0:14:11.74,Main,PatchKurumi,0,0,0,,What a wonderful retort.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.17,0:14:15.00,Main,PatchKurumi,0,0,0,,I'm truly blessed.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.64,0:14:32.30,Main,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(640,1)\fnArial\fs10\shad0\bord0\frz12.36\pos(304,188.666)\c&HFAF7EA&}Wednesday, February 15th
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.76,0:14:32.30,Main,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(640,1)\fnArial\fs10\shad0\bord0\frz12.36\c&H454545&\pos(315.2,231.866)}You have a new message.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.30,0:14:33.01,Main,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fnArial\fs10\shad0\bord0\frz12.36\c&H676767&\pos(237.333,141.733)}Kotori
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.30,0:14:33.01,Main,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fnArial\fs8\shad0\bord0\frz12.36\c&HA57467&\pos(282.133,102.8)}Today
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.30,0:14:33.01,Main,Sign,0,0,0,,{\an7\fnArial\fs10\shad0\bord0\frz12.36\c&H676767&\pos(242.133,194.533)}Reine, come to the meeting room\NWe have an emergency.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.55,0:14:35.80,Main,Reine,0,0,0,,You're coming, Wizard?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.94,0:14:38.89,Main,Kotori,0,0,0,,The situation is dire.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.41,0:14:40.80,Main,Kotori,0,0,0,,Judging from the state of things,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.80,0:14:44.52,Main,Kotori,0,0,0,,the information we received from \NKurumi's clone is worth believing.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.93,0:14:48.97,Main,Kotori,0,0,0,,Though we also can't afford \Nto run and hide forever.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.97,0:14:51.92,Main,Kaguya,0,0,0,,But there's no negotiating either.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.92,0:14:52.66,Main,Yuzuru,0,0,0,,Certainly.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.00,0:14:55.16,Main,Yuzuru,0,0,0,,There's no room for discussion here.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.54,0:14:56.67,Main,Tohka,0,0,0,,Which means...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.67,0:14:58.29,Main,Kotori,0,0,0,,We only have one option left.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.75,0:15:00.54,Main,Kotori,0,0,0,,Defeating DEM.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.85,0:15:03.79,Main,Kotori,0,0,0,,Of course, that's easier said than done.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.17,0:15:07.17,Main,Kotori,0,0,0,,But we'll have to go on the offensive
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.80,0:15:10.33,Main,Kotori,0,0,0,,in order to seize our own future.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.33,0:15:12.91,Main - Italics,Woodman,0,0,0,,That's right, Commander Itsuka.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.30,0:15:14.67,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,Mr. Woodman!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.56,0:15:18.20,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,Are you feeling better already?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.20,0:15:21.81,Main - Italics,Woodman,0,0,0,,Yes, you don't need to worry about me.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.09,0:15:25.50,Main - Italics,Woodman,0,0,0,,I'm sorry I was out of contact for so long.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.89,0:15:29.55,Main - Italics,Woodman,0,0,0,,Our enemy is certainly great.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.55,0:15:34.76,Main - Italics,Woodman,0,0,0,,However, DEM is an organization helmed
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.76,0:15:39.70,Main - Italics,Woodman,0,0,0,,by Isaac Westcott's charisma \Nand Ellen Mathers's competence.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.70,0:15:45.84,Main - Italics,Woodman,0,0,0,,That means it won't be much of a threat \Nonce those two are taken out.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.11,0:15:50.57,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,In other words, defeating Westcott \Nand Ellen is our key to victory.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.21,0:15:52.52,Main - Italics,MARIA,0,0,0,,Understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.52,0:15:55.97,Main - Italics,MARIA,0,0,0,,Then perhaps it would be worth trying {\i0}that{\i1}.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.97,0:15:57.03,Main,Shido,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.03,0:15:59.10,Main,Kotori,0,0,0,,MARIA, what do you mean by "that"?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.10,0:16:04.35,Main - Italics,MARIA,0,0,0,,I'm saying that it might be \Npossible to nullify Nibeelcole.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.35,0:16:05.16,Main,Nia,0,0,0,,Huh?!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.64,0:16:09.37,Main,Origami,0,0,0,,Truthfully, I also have an idea \Nfor how to handle Bandersnatch.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.37,0:16:10.61,Main,Nia,0,0,0,,H-Hold on!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.61,0:16:12.10,Main,Orgami,0,0,0,,The enemy's new Realizer models are—
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.10,0:16:13.62,Main,Nia,0,0,0,,Stop, stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.62,0:16:15.12,Main,Nia,0,0,0,,Enough talking about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.52,0:16:17.46,Main - Italics,MARIA,0,0,0,,What's the matter, Nia?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.46,0:16:19.62,Main - Italics,MARIA,0,0,0,,We're just getting to the main topic.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.62,0:16:21.15,Main,Nia,0,0,0,,Tsk, tsk, tsk.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.15,0:16:23.85,Main,Nia,0,0,0,,You don't get it, Robo-girl.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.85,0:16:27.25,Main - Italics,MARIA,0,0,0,,First, I demand an explanation \Nfor that nickname.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.25,0:16:29.75,Main - Italics,MARIA,0,0,0,,Depending on your answer, \NI may eject you from the ship.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.75,0:16:31.17,Main,Nia,0,0,0,,Have you forgotten?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.17,0:16:34.38,Main,Nia,0,0,0,,Westcott can use Beelzebub, \Nthe omniscient Demon King.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.38,0:16:35.14,Main,Kotori,0,0,0,,Ah!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.50,0:16:36.76,Main,Natsumi,0,0,0,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.76,0:16:40.38,Main,Natsumi,0,0,0,,He can look up any event that happens \Nthroughout the entire universe.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.38,0:16:41.91,Main,Natsumi,0,0,0,,Meaning...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.91,0:16:46.02,Main,Yoshino,0,0,0,,He might learn everything \Nthat unfolds in this discussion.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.02,0:16:47.85,Main,Nia,0,0,0,,Exactly.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.85,0:16:48.78,Main,Nia,0,0,0,,However,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.78,0:16:51.48,Main,Nia,0,0,0,,it doesn't know how to read people's minds
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.48,0:16:53.56,Main,Nia,0,0,0,,or what the future holds.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.56,0:16:55.86,Main,Nia,0,0,0,,So even if you come up with a strategy,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.86,0:16:57.91,Main,Nia,0,0,0,,you can't mention it out loud.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.58,0:17:00.89,Main - Italics,MARIA,0,0,0,,I hate to admit it, but you are correct.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.25,0:17:02.98,Main - Italics,MARIA,0,0,0,,Thank you, Nia.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.16,0:17:06.97,Main,Nia,0,0,0,,As long as you understand!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.97,0:17:08.67,Main,Nia,0,0,0,,Humility is a virtue,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.18,0:17:11.38,Main,Nia,0,0,0,,spriteless Robo-girl.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.01,0:17:15.96,Main - Italics,MARIA,0,0,0,,By the way, Nia, could you \Nplease touch my console?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.96,0:17:17.30,Main,Nia,0,0,0,,Huh? Like this?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.55,0:17:24.77,Main,Nia,0,0,0,,Hey! What are you doing?! Come on!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.77,0:17:27.37,Main - Italics,MARIA,0,0,0,,I'm grateful for the flaw you pointed out.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.37,0:17:32.52,Main - Italics,MARIA,0,0,0,,However, you needed to be punished \Nfor that insulting nickname.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.32,0:17:35.28,Main,Nia,0,0,0,,That's false logic!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.57,0:17:38.26,Main,Miku,0,0,0,,Still, it's rather absurd that we have to have
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.26,0:17:42.06,Main,Miku,0,0,0,,our strategy meeting without being \Nable to voice any ideas or opinions.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.06,0:17:44.70,Main,Origami,0,0,0,,I think there are still things \Nwe can each do on our own.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:45.18,0:17:47.17,Main,Origami,0,0,0,,There's something I'd like to take care of, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.17,0:17:48.69,Main - Italics,Woodman,0,0,0,,Good point.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.69,0:17:51.67,Main - Italics,Woodman,0,0,0,,I'll do everything I can as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.05,0:17:58.58,Main,Kurumi,0,0,0,,Do you have any excuse for yourself?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.58,0:17:59.84,Main,PatchKurumi,0,0,0,,My, oh my.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.22,0:18:03.60,Main,Kurumi,0,0,0,,I already received word from another me.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.88,0:18:09.35,Main,Kurumi,0,0,0,,I heard you informed Shido \Nand Kotori about DEM's assault.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.67,0:18:13.78,Main,Kurumi,0,0,0,,I can't have you acting on your own \Nwithout orders from me.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.42,0:18:19.06,Main,Kurumi,0,0,0,,You'll need to pay for disturbing \Nthe order with your life.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.72,0:18:23.49,Main,PatchKurumi,0,0,0,,Yes, yes. There's no getting past that.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.85,0:18:26.46,Main,PatchKurumi,0,0,0,,But one last thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.24,0:18:29.62,Main,PatchKurumi,0,0,0,,I have a message from Shido.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.13,0:18:35.09,Main,PatchKurumi,0,0,0,,"I love, love, super-love you! \NLet's get married, my honey!"
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.09,0:18:38.26,Main,Kurumi,0,0,0,,Only the "my honey" part of that was accurate!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.86,0:18:43.96,Main,PatchKurumi,0,0,0,,I know you already heard it \Nfrom another clone.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.88,0:18:53.67,Main,PatchKurumi,0,0,0,,My, oh my.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.30,0:18:55.70,Main,Kurumi,0,0,0,,I wouldn't be so foolish
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.70,0:18:58.97,Main,Kurumi,0,0,0,,as to pare down my own forces \Nright before a major battle.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.28,0:19:02.20,Main,Kurumi,0,0,0,,If you are still a part of me,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.20,0:19:04.03,Main,Kurumi,0,0,0,,then at least be useful first
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.52,0:19:06.79,Main,Kurumi,0,0,0,,and then die on the battlefield for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.77,0:19:14.31,Main,PatchKurumi,0,0,0,,Yes, yes. I understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.95,0:19:19.30,Main,Ryoko,0,0,0,,A secret organization protecting Spirits, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.64,0:19:21.45,Main,Ryoko,0,0,0,,You show up out of nowhere,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.45,0:19:23.43,Main,Ryoko,0,0,0,,and you expect us to believe that nonsense?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:23.43,0:19:25.31,Main,Mikie,0,0,0,,B-But Captain,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.31,0:19:29.14,Main,Mikie,0,0,0,,they've both come here \Nknowing it meant great danger.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.14,0:19:32.44,Main,Milly,0,0,0,,I don't think we should be \Nso quick to assume they're lying.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.44,0:19:35.33,Main,Mana,0,0,0,,I know you must find it hard to believe.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:35.33,0:19:38.76,Main,Mana,0,0,0,,But it's all true.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.76,0:19:40.11,Main,Origami,0,0,0,,On February 20th,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.11,0:19:43.32,Main,Origami,0,0,0,,there will likely be a major \Nbattle here in Tengu City.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.65,0:19:44.67,Main,Origami,0,0,0,,When it goes down,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.67,0:19:48.67,Main,Origami,0,0,0,,DEM will probably request \Neven the captains sortie.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.34,0:19:51.71,Main,Origami,0,0,0,,But I want you to ignore that request.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:52.09,0:19:57.32,Main,Milly,0,0,0,,Is that also information uncovered \Nby the secret organization Ratatoskr?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.32,0:20:00.41,Main,Mikie,0,0,0,,Still, even if what you say is true...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.41,0:20:01.22,Main,Ryoko,0,0,0,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.53,0:20:06.60,Main,Ryoko,0,0,0,,Spurning DEM's request means \Nignoring orders from above.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.98,0:20:11.64,Main,Ryoko,0,0,0,,So you're asking us to lose our jobs \Nand serve prison time on top of that?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:11.64,0:20:12.94,Main,Ryoko,0,0,0,,For one thing,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.33,0:20:16.67,Main,Ryoko,0,0,0,,why are you telling us \Nnot to attack the Spirits?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.67,0:20:18.48,Main,Ryoko,0,0,0,,They're the enemy of mankind, aren't they?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.48,0:20:22.75,Main,Origami,0,0,0,,That's maliciously spun \Ninformation spread by DEM.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.75,0:20:26.20,Main,Mana,0,0,0,,The Spirits have no intention \Nof attacking mankind.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:27.74,0:20:30.59,Main,Mikie,0,0,0,,That's a lot to take in all at once.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.35,0:20:34.94,Main,Milly,0,0,0,,If what you just told us is true,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.94,0:20:39.61,Main,Milly,0,0,0,,then I would love to try fiddling with this \Nsecret organization's new weapons!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.61,0:20:41.84,Main,Milly,0,0,0,,It's stirring my instincts as a mechanic!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.84,0:20:44.13,Main,Ryoko,0,0,0,,Sorry, but could you be quiet for a bit?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:48.29,0:20:50.89,Main,Ryoko,0,0,0,,You know we can't do what you're asking.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.28,0:20:52.81,Main,Mikie,0,0,0,,Captain...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.81,0:20:53.90,Main,Origami,0,0,0,,That's a shame.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.90,0:20:56.15,Main,Origami,0,0,0,,Though I don't fault you for your decision.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:56.42,0:20:59.30,Main,Origami,0,0,0,,Still, if you do deploy to the battlefield,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:59.30,0:21:00.98,Main,Origami,0,0,0,,at least stick to the rear.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.98,0:21:01.53,Main,Ryoko,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.31,0:21:04.03,Main,Origami,0,0,0,,I don't want to kill you all.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.03,0:21:07.25,Main,Ryoko,0,0,0,,Sounds like you're really\Nunderestimating us.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.25,0:21:09.12,Main,Ryoko,0,0,0,,I know you were a skilled fighter, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.05,0:21:12.95,Main,Origami,0,0,0,,Please.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.12,0:21:31.35,Main,Kurumi,0,0,0,,Zaphkiel, Het!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:31.58,0:21:32.18,Main,Kurumi,0,0,0,,Het!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.43,0:21:33.43,Main,Kurumi,0,0,0,,Het!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:33.68,0:21:34.56,Main,Kurumi,0,0,0,,Het!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.56,0:21:40.32,Main,Kurumi,0,0,0,,Het, Het, Het, Het, Het, Het,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.67,0:21:41.66,Main,Kurumi,0,0,0,,Het!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:47.24,0:21:52.95,Main,Kurumi,0,0,0,,Now, shall we begin our Date?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:52.95,0:21:54.95,Main,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fnTimes New Roman\b1\fs20\shad1\blur1\bord1\c&H000000&\3c&HADB0AD&\4c&HADB0AD&\pos(317.333,185.466)}Episode 1
Dialogue: 0,0:21:52.95,0:21:54.95,Main,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fnTimes New Roman\an8\b1\fs20\shad1\blur1\bord1\c&H000000&\3c&HADB0AD&\4c&HADB0AD&\pos(317.866,280.399)}Beginnings of War
Dialogue: 0,0:23:24.96,0:23:39.98,Main,Sign,0,0,0,,{\an3\fnTimes New Roman\bord1\blur3\shad1\fs16\pos(604,309.733)\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H5B5B5B&\4c&H5B5B5B&}Episode 2   "Final Respite"
Dialogue: 0,0:23:25.83,0:23:28.44,Main - Top,Narrator,0,0,0,,The big battle against DEM draws near,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:28.44,0:23:30.51,Main - Top,Narrator,0,0,0,,with everyone harboring different feelings
Dialogue: 0,0:23:30.51,0:23:32.44,Main - Top,Narrator,0,0,0,,as they spend what time remains.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:32.84,0:23:35.47,Main - Top,Narrator,0,0,0,,Next time is episode 2, "Final Respite."
Dialogue: 0,0:23:35.97,0:23:38.91,Main - Top,Narrator,0,0,0,,The curtain rises on {\i1}Date A Live{\i0} season 5!
